            "fills": [
              {
                "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                "fillOpacity": 1
              }
            ],
            "fontFamily": "Arimo"
          },
          {
            "lineHeight": "1.35",
            "fontStyle": "normal",
            "children": [
              {
                "lineHeight": "1.35",
                "fontStyle": "normal",
                "textTransform": "none",
                "textAlign": "left",
                "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
                "fontSize": "28",
                "fontWeight": "400",
                "textDirection": "ltr",
                "fontVariantId": "normal-400",
                "textDecoration": "none",
                "letterSpacing": "0",
                "fills": [
                  {
                    "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Arimo",
                "text": "\u00f72 and \u00d72 (#1936, D4), after the tempo steps on Tempo & click: the loop read as half or twice its bars, at half or twice the tempo, the audio as it is. Live only for a tempo derived from the loop and not retimed since, whole bars, one shared loop, no take recording; halving needs an even bar count, and the tempo stays in 30 to 300 BPM. The readout's Loop panel has the same pair beside its tempo (page 25, 12 \/ loop-panel-derived-tempo)."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
            "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
